    "ConvertAssign": {
      "rust": "rust_stdlib::database::sql::convert_assign",
      "deviation": "closed-interface+type-name-text",
      "note": "dest is &mut dyn Scanner and src a driver::Value; UUID is a destination as in Go, and a Value::Decimal source composes into any driver::Compose destination. A driver.Rows cursor source (into *Rows) cannot be expressed because driver::Value is a closed enum. Go formats a decimal source with the application type's %v and names it by %T; Rust holds only the decomposed parts, so it uses driver::Decimal's General Decimal Arithmetic text and the name driver.Decimal. A driver::Compose destination that rejects a source is named by std::any::type_name (a Rust path), where Go prints *pkg.Type."
    },
